infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Index Scan vs Seq Scan: cost flips with selectivity
  desc Same 1M-row table — the planner picks by cost, and selectivity decides the winner
  compares
    - label Index Scan — random_page_cost x matching_rows
      children
        - label 100 rows match -> cost 400
          desc 100 x 4.0 random fetches — 37x cheaper than Seq Scan, so Index Scan wins
        - label 100,000 rows match -> cost 400,000
          desc 100,000 x 4.0 random fetches — far past the 15,000 Seq Scan cost, so it loses
        - label Crossover at ~5-15% of rows
          desc Above this fraction random heap hops cost more than reading the whole heap
    - label Seq Scan — relpages + reltuples (fixed)
      children
        - label Constant cost 15,000
          desc 5000 pages x 1.0 + 1M tuples x 0.01 — independent of how many rows match
        - label Wins on low selectivity
          desc Most rows match: one sequential pass beats hundreds of thousands of random fetches
        - label Loses on high selectivity
          desc 100 matching rows cost only 400 via the index — 37x below the 15,000 floor
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
